{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions","id":262986,"title":"Newbie hunter questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-22T11:58:52-07:00","id":262986,"title":"Newbie hunter questions","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> I have just gotten into the WoD series and ive been reading the rulebook's processes of creating a character.<br /> <br /> though I was stumped when I got to the area where it talks about putting knots in your character's Physical, Mental and Social fields, even more stumped when I saw the character sheet.<br /> <br /> my question is: How do I know how many knots I can fill? I mean I know it states that 5 requires 2 knots, but where do my knots come from? Do I have a certain number of knots I start out with like Skill Points in D20 D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> please help me out.<br /> <br /> (PS: I will probably be using this thread to post more questions should any come up)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:04:37-07:00","id":263004,"title":"","content":"Hi! Welcome to the World of Darkness. Hunter's a great game, I hope you get a lot of enjoyment out of it. Since you put this in the Hunter subforum, it's possible that you might have missed something important, and I apologize if my guess is wrong: the first edition New World of Darkness gamebooks require the World of Darkness Core Rulebook, the one that looks like <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1124/World-of-Darkness-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. If you just have the Hunter corebook alone, you don't have the full ruleset.<br /> <br /> If you are, in fact, talking about the Core Rulebook, the character creation rules in the beginning of the book should tell you how many dots you have to distribute among Attributes and Skills. Each Attribute begins with 1 dot (the dots you have available to distribute do not include these free first dots) and can be increased to a maximum of 5. Each Skill begins with 0 dots and can be increased to a maximum of 5.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask any other questions that come up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T13:23:10-07:00","id":263047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=263004#post263004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Welcome to the World of Darkness. Hunter's a great game, I hope you get a lot of enjoyment out of it. Since you put this in the Hunter subforum, it's possible that you might have missed something important, and I apologize if my guess is wrong: the first edition New World of Darkness gamebooks require the World of Darkness Core Rulebook, the one that looks like <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1124/World-of-Darkness-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. If you just have the Hunter corebook alone, you don't have the full ruleset.<br /> <br /> If you are, in fact, talking about the Core Rulebook, the character creation rules in the beginning of the book should tell you how many dots you have to distribute among Attributes and Skills. Each Attribute begins with 1 dot (the dots you have available to distribute do not include these free first dots) and can be increased to a maximum of 5. Each Skill begins with 0 dots and can be increased to a maximum of 5.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask any other questions that come up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I do have the core rules, but even that was unclear, it doesnt tell me how many dots i start out with to spend at 1st level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:24:16-07:00","id":263116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranatosk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=263047#post263047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I do have the core rules, but even that was unclear, it doesnt tell me how many dots i start out with to spend at 1st level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Core Rulebook page 34, and it's duplicated on page 55 of the Vigil book. In both cases it's on the left column of the page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T04:31:17-07:00","id":264496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=263116#post263116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core Rulebook page 34, and it's duplicated on page 55 of the Vigil book. In both cases it's on the left column of the page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I think Ive found it.<br /> <br /> Primary: 11 points<br /> <br /> Secondary: 7 points<br /> <br /> Tertiary: 4 points.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help, was completely lost and confused and now im back on track. :3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T15:27:11-07:00","id":264915,"title":"","content":"you do know that all spending information is at the bottom of the character sheet at the back of the book right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Do the dead dare walk the Earth before my eyes? Will the undead raise an army, fall in, and advance? Will those who would abandon God and embrace the heretical order DARE to presume to meet my gaze!? Iscariot will not allow it. <b>I</b> will not allow it.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3889-ninjasantaclause","name":"Ninjasantaclause","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T13:29:05-07:00","id":267656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ninjasantaclause</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=264915#post264915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you do know that all spending information is at the bottom of the character sheet at the back of the book right?</div> </div> </div> </div>actually im using a PDF i found, but thanks for the info <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> actually one more question: what does it mean by -3/-1 unskilled? does that mean I remove how many im unskilled in or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","user":"Ranatosk","date":". 09-28-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T14:45:27-07:00","id":267683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranatosk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=267656#post267656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> actually im using a PDF i found, but thanks for the info <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> actually one more question: what does it mean by -3/-1 unskilled? does that mean I remove how many im unskilled in or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it means that if you attempt a roll involving a skill that you have no dots in, you subtract that many dice from the pool for your roll (mental skills -3 unskilled, physical and social skills -1 unskilled).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T15:47:35-07:00","id":267731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=267683#post267683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it means that if you attempt a roll involving a skill that you have no dots in, you subtract that many dice from the pool for your roll (mental skills -3 unskilled, physical and social skills -1 unskilled).</div> </div> </div> </div>thats not exactly what i meant, but thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T18:56:33-07:00","id":267830,"title":"","content":"For Attributes you start with 1 dot in each of the nine, these are seperated into mental, physical and social, just like skills are. You then get 5, 4 and 3 dots to spend for the three categories.<br /> <br /> The 11, 7 and 4 dots are what you place in the skill categories. Whilst Attributes get a free dot in each, skills always start at zero dots.<br /> <br /> When you make a skill roll, it's generally done with an Attribute and that makes the number of dice you roll in your dicepool. If you use a skill you have zero dots in, the unskilled penalty is the dice removed from your Attribute which you would roll alone in that case to make your dicepool up.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps you out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T19:13:11-07:00","id":269718,"title":"","content":"Another question: Experience point costs.<br /> <br /> It says that in order to increase an attribute by 1 Knot it requires 20xp and the 5th requires 25xp, but it doesnt say how much it costs for skills, merits and other stuff involving knots.<br /> <br /> so how much does it cost to increase skills, merits and stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T04:51:50-07:00","id":270048,"title":"","content":"Attributes cost new dots x5, Merits are new rating x2, Morality is new rating x3, Skills are new rating x3, specialties cost 3xp and willpower costs 8xp.<br /> <br /> When you use experience to go up more than one level, you need to buy the levels between. This means if you're raising an Attribute you have at 2 to 4 dots, you need to buy it at 3 dots (15xp) and then at 4 dots (+20xp, for a total of 35xp from 2 dots). You couldn't just spend 25xp to boost an attribute from 2 dots to 5 for example. At least thats how I always read the experience costs for nwod, I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> In the God-Machine update there is no escalating cost and things have a straight cost thats the same for each level, but unless you have Mortal Remains, Hunter:the Vigil uses the standard nwod rules, at least until a Hunter 2nd edition comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T12:04:57-07:00","id":270266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=270048#post270048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attributes cost new dots x5, Merits are new rating x2, Morality is new rating x3, Skills are new rating x3, specialties cost 3xp and willpower costs 8xp.<br /> <br /> When you use experience to go up more than one level, you need to buy the levels between. This means if you're raising an Attribute you have at 2 to 4 dots, you need to buy it at 3 dots (15xp) and then at 4 dots (+20xp, for a total of 35xp from 2 dots). You couldn't just spend 25xp to boost an attribute from 2 dots to 5 for example. At least thats how I always read the experience costs for nwod, I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> In the God-Machine update there is no escalating cost and things have a straight cost thats the same for each level, but unless you have Mortal Remains, Hunter:the Vigil uses the standard nwod rules, at least until a Hunter 2nd edition comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>okay, but what about other stuff like skills and Merits? Does it cost the same as raising attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T13:22:34-07:00","id":271036,"title":"","content":"Yes for both, you need to buy each level before paying for the next. Say you got Resources 1 (a one dot merit) and you want to raise it up to three, then you'd need to spend 4xp to raise it to 2, then 6xp for 3, a total of 10xp to raise it from 1 to 3.<br /> Skills are the same, if you got a skill at 1 dot, you pay 6xp for them to be 2 dots, then 9xp to get them to 3, etc. Buying one dot in a skill you don't have at all would cost 3xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:43:29-07:00","id":271120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=271036#post271036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes for both, you need to buy each level before paying for the next. Say you got Resources 1 (a one dot merit) and you want to raise it up to three, then you'd need to spend 4xp to raise it to 2, then 6xp for 3, a total of 10xp to raise it from 1 to 3.<br /> Skills are the same, if you got a skill at 1 dot, you pay 6xp for them to be 2 dots, then 9xp to get them to 3, etc. Buying one dot in a skill you don't have at all would cost 3xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clearing that up for me.<br /> <br /> one more question: Starting money.<br /> <br /> ive looked through the manuals and it doesnt say anything about how much money you start out with nor does it give you a section of the book showing what you can buy. I dont want my character to be completely defenseless and vulnerable, so how do I go about doing this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","user":"Ranatosk","date":". 10-02-2014, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T12:03:46-07:00","id":271671,"title":"","content":"Thats not something that has specific ruling in nwod past the Resources Merit. Mainly I've seen it house-ruled that you can have gear up to your Resources dots or maybe gear can be worth +1 dot. The number of items you can hold is really what makes sense for your character to have.<br /> <br /> If you look at the sample gear in either the Core or in Hunter, there are no price costs, each item is worth a number of dots or zero dots. Simple answer; Take a look at the items and give your char what would make most sense for them to have and what you think they would have given their circumstances, background and concept.<br /> <br /> The gear-lists are located in the Core at pages 139-141 and armour and weapons are on p.169-170. Hunter has gear mainly placed on pages 229-253. Endowment rules start on p.150 if you got a Hunter that can have them and spent the Merit dots to snag them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T15:37:02-07:00","id":272534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=271671#post271671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats not something that has specific ruling in nwod past the Resources Merit. Mainly I've seen it house-ruled that you can have gear up to your Resources dots or maybe gear can be worth +1 dot. The number of items you can hold is really what makes sense for your character to have.<br /> <br /> If you look at the sample gear in either the Core or in Hunter, there are no price costs, each item is worth a number of dots or zero dots. Simple answer; Take a look at the items and give your char what would make most sense for them to have and what you think they would have given their circumstances, background and concept.<br /> <br /> The gear-lists are located in the Core at pages 139-141 and armour and weapons are on p.169-170. Hunter has gear mainly placed on pages 229-253. Endowment rules start on p.150 if you got a Hunter that can have them and spent the Merit dots to snag them.</div> </div> </div> </div>so i have no way to determine what my character has until my first game session?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T21:19:46-07:00","id":272697,"title":"","content":"you could create a list of the equipment you would like your character to own and then ask the ST if it's kosher at some point in time before the game session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:13:01-07:00","id":272965,"title":"","content":"Seconded on what Leaper said... Thats pretty much the way I've always done it in each nwod game I've ever played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T05:33:55-07:00","id":273663,"title":"","content":"Well, thanks everyone. :3<br /> <br /> (im still gonna use this for questions, unless it dies of inactivity, so ill make a new one if that happens)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T07:00:30-07:00","id":273778,"title":"","content":"The general assumption of the nWoD is the player characters are all roughly middle class. You have a car, house/apartment, etc. without needing to pay for it. If you have a relevant job, you could even claim some basic weapons and armor (my last character was an active-duty cop; I started with a light pistol, nightstick and bulletproof vest. By finding my cruiser I added an AP carbine and shotgun to my loadout)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:55:43-07:00","id":274076,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that the assumption is that they're middle class so much as they're getting by; to whatever standard fits the character/setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:52:31-07:00","id":274724,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I've played plenty of Hunters who were extremely well-off, if not rich. And the resources that came with it...ohhhhhh man.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:27:29-07:00","id":275020,"title":"","content":"Well now in GMC 'Housing' comes under the gear-list, so make sure you have a dot or few in that item <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also I'm pretty sure I saw in some book somewhere vehicles with dot costs next to them, though as I look at my Corebook at least, I cannot see them being priced in their statblocks there... Hm.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you could play a homeless guy with no Resource dots and no Housing dots in GMC rules now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:43:23-07:00","id":282291,"title":"","content":"I just started STing a game where I ended up allowing 3 x Resources in equipment, plus 3 x dots in Status for equipment you don't own (Police car etc.) Seemed about right, although the PCs technically don't own <i>houses</i> right now (they wouldn't be at home anyway for this Chapter.)<br /> <br /> Maybe allow 4x or 5x dots if your characters are &quot;dug in&quot; at home in a city somewhere.<br /> <br /> You can find prices for commercially-available vehicles <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Vehicles\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:27:37-07:00","id":287600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=282291#post282291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just started STing a game where I ended up allowing 3 x Resources in equipment, plus 3 x dots in Status for equipment you don't own (Police car etc.) Seemed about right, although the PCs technically don't own <i>houses</i> right now (they wouldn't be at home anyway for this Chapter.)<br /> <br /> Maybe allow 4x or 5x dots if your characters are &quot;dug in&quot; at home in a city somewhere.<br /> <br /> You can find prices for commercially-available vehicles <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Vehicles\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>*reads the list* Motorcycles are free? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> *squee*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:57:43-07:00","id":287635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranatosk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=287600#post287600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Motorcycles are free? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> *squee*</div> </div> </div> </div>But sadly, they don't have room for anyone to ride them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T05:09:40-07:00","id":288459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=287635#post287635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But sadly, they don't have room for anyone to ride them.</div> </div> </div> </div>who says im gonna be hitching anyone? get your own ride, i dont wanna be &quot;The Driver&quot; of the group. Im just giving something my character to use in order to get around.<br /> <br /> for free :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3925-ranatosk","name":"Ranatosk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T03:58:59-07:00","id":289417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranatosk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=288459#post288459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> who says im gonna be hitching anyone? get your own ride, i dont wanna be &quot;The Driver&quot; of the group. Im just giving something my character to use in order to get around.<br /> <br /> for free :3</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they literally don't have the capacity listed for <i>anyone</i>. Not even the driver <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T10:41:41-07:00","id":289714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranatosk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=287600#post287600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *reads the list* Motorcycles are free? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> *squee*</div> </div> </div> </div>:P<br /> <br /> For some reason the WoD vehicle table did not include resource costs.<br /> This does not make motorcycles more free than any other kind of equipment that doesn't have a listed cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T13:54:45-07:00","id":289964,"title":"","content":"I will just ask here.<br /> <br /> It's okay to render non-Awakened Sorcery just with Witchfinders? I need Endowments for my Hunter conspiracy as they draw some of their powers from rituals passed down through generations through fae related legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T14:07:19-07:00","id":290779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/262986-newbie-hunter-questions?p=289964#post289964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will just ask here.<br /> <br /> It's okay to render non-Awakened Sorcery just with Witchfinders? I need Endowments for my Hunter conspiracy as they draw some of their powers from rituals passed down through generations through fae related legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what its there for. You might like Second Sight (from the core WoD line) for a more detailed look at ritual / folk magic as well as psychic phenomena but Witchfinders is a big deconstruction of magic in all its forms so you should be good to go if you already have a strong idea on the lore for your conspiracy's endowments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T06:52:58-07:00","id":291305,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member